1200 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: We arrived ahead of schedule, so only a few rooms are ready. The\dining room and my room are clean, so we can live here for a while.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1210 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: If it weren't for the King of the North, this would have been our fun\holiday. Why does it have to be like this...?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1220 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: It's ready. You must be starving, we've been on the run since last\night.":GOSUB 5100
1230 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David had no appetite; he could feel the King of the North breathing down\his neck. But once Susanna placed a plate in front of him, he started\eating ravenously.":GOSUB 5100
1240 BM$="After the meal, David started feeling sleepy; and yet, he did not want to\sleep, fearing he might have another nightmare.":GOSUB 5100
1250 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: Now that I'm full, I'm feeling sleepy. Why don't we both sleep in my\room?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1260 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I'm sleepy as well, but I'm afraid I'm going to have another\nightmare... Promise me to wake me up if you think I'm having one.":GOSUB 5100
1270 COMMON FO:GOSUB 6110:BM$="David and Susanna went to sleep in their room.":GOSUB 5100
1275 GOSUB 9010:'
