1600 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: It's about Greg, he... He's dead. It must have been the King of the\North's deathly curse.":GOSUB 5100
1610 BM$="Lands: I called him, and he said he'd come as soon as possible. But he was\taking too long, and I was worried... Then he called me on the phone.":GOSUB 5100
1620 BM$="Lands: He was calling from a restaurant outside Haworth. He said he\noticed a car tailing him. I told him to stay there and that I'd come to him\instead.":GOSUB 5100
1630 BM$="Lands: He told me not to come, that it was too dangerous, and hung up. I\decided to go anyway, and drove towards that restaurant.":GOSUB 5100
1640 BM$="Lands: Then I... I found him, right at the entrance of Haworth. His car was\smashed, and he was dead. I didn't see anyone nearby, but there's never\been any robberies around these parts.":GOSUB 5100
1650 BM$="Lands: He was killed by northern tribesmen, I'm sure of it. Susanna, you and\David must leave at once. There's no time for discussions. You have to\leave England before it's too late.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1660 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: That's impossible... I left my passport at the office.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1670 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: Let's go back to London. If we floor it, the King of the North\shouldn't be able to catch us.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1680 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: Nonsense. You should go to Scotland instead. You can have your\passports mailed to you, and then leave the country by boat.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1690 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: What should we do, David? Do you want to run from the King of\the North...?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1700 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: I'm willing to go to the other side of the planet to live with you.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1710 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: I hate the idea of running away without a fight... What about all\the dark sorcerers who gave their lives for us?":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1720 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: We were born to protect the bloodline. I, too, am willing to give my\life to prevent the northern tribesmen from following you. That is our\fate.":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1730 GOSUB 6300:BM$="David: You shouldn't be throwing your life away for us! Nobody should have\to die like this... Damn it! If it weren't for the King of the North...!":GOSUB 5100:RETURN
1740 GOSUB 6330:BM$="Lands: It is your fate to run, David. If you oppose fate, your blood will be\severed, and the soul of King Hroth will wander aimlessly for all eternity.":GOSUB 5100
1750 BM$="David did not care about fate, and would rather avenge the deaths of all\the sorcerers who died for his sake. However, when he saw Lands's tears\rolling down his cheeks, he remained silent.":GOSUB 5100:BM$="He could not insult Lands's resolve like that.":GOSUB 5100
1760 GOSUB 6310:BM$="Susanna: It's up to you, David. We were all born to follow you. Your will is\King Hroth's will.":GOSUB 5100
1770 GOSUB 6300:BM$="After listening to Susanna's words, David knew that making this choice\was also fate.":GOSUB 5100
